# Claims in someone else's kit (docs/DIALOGUE.md, "Claims in someone else's kit"): you're claiming
# only when you pick the claim. The look decides it (its score is shown before you pick); a passed
# look waves you through this post, and buys nothing else. The true answer costs nothing.

conv post.bastion.claim
for post:bastion
when kit:in_kit & !caught
topic "Answer as one of theirs."
prio quest
voice bastion

node start
  say "You. Which unit? I don't know your face."
  > @claim "One of yours. Let me through." -> passed | caught   check look bastion 2
  > @truth "Off a dead man. I'm not one of yours." -> honest
  > @leave "Never mind." -> hub

node passed
  say "Fine. Go on. Keep your head down, we're short of heads."
  do call:post_wave
  > @back1 "Something else." -> hub

node caught
  say "Hands on the barrier. That kit goes back where it came from."
  > @back2 "Understood." -> hub

node honest
  say "At least you said so. Take it off before somebody less patient asks."
  > @back3 "Something else." -> hub

conv post.redhand.claim
for post:redhand
when kit:in_kit & !caught
topic "Say you're crew."
prio quest
voice redhand

node start
  say "Crew? Funny. I know all the crew. What do they call you?"
  > @claim "One of yours. Wave me on." -> passed | caught   check look redhand 2
  > @truth "Found the armband. Thought it'd help." -> honest
  > @leave "Never mind." -> hub

node passed
  say "Huh. Must be new. Go on, then, and pay next time like everyone."
  do call:post_wave
  > @back1 "Something else." -> hub

node caught
  say "Lads! Dress-up day. Armband off, if you please."
  > @back2 "Fair enough." -> hub

node honest
  say "It might, too. Not here. Here we count the armbands."
  > @back3 "Something else." -> hub
